    docs(cfta-generator): a Binders language is cyclic only with a subterm rule
    
    The README, the Typing module and the changelog said that a Binders bound
    makes the automaton cyclic, so its ranks are size-major. A Binders language
    whose rules have no subterm is finite. Its automaton is acyclic, and its
    ranks follow the constructor order: with only the rules
    FixA (value (PayP (PayP PayZ))) and FixB (value 0) under Binders 0,
    values gives the size-4 FixA term before the size-2 FixB term. The docs now
    qualify the claim and advise upToSize for that case too.

